LOCAL CHAINING AND CONSTRUCTOR CHAINING

Super method is always the first line of the constructor regardless of whether programmer has explicitly written it or not.
Super method takes the control to the constructor of the direct parent class , this is also known as constructor chaining. In other words constructor
chaining is the process of the calling constructor of the direct parent class using super class. In only case, when the programmer has explicitly written or
called this method super will not be the first line of the constructor. This method can be used to call constructor of the same class, the process of calling
the constructor from another constructor of the same class by using this method is also known as local chaining. Both this method as well as super method have
to be the first line of constructor. Hence inside a constructor we can either call this or super method. 
 

