ArrayList is efficient if we insert data at the rear end, if we insert data at particular position or in between or data is inserted at the 
beginning of the list then arraylist is not efficient. 
TO overcome this disadvantage of arraylist of have to make use of arrayDeque.

ArrayDeque - it internally make use of doubly ended queue data structure. The doubly ended queue as the name suggest will have two ends. one
at the front and one more at the rare which makes the insertion of data very efficient from both the ends.
  
To overcome the disadvantage of arraydeque(intermediate insertion not possible) we have to make use of linkedlist data structure. Linkedlist 
 is efficient in the front insertion, in the rare insertion as well as the element at any intermediate position. 
 
When an arrayDeque is implemented as queue and linkedlist is implemented as stack, ll is more effiecient. 


