WHat is the advantages of Iterator?
while reading the content in the structure, concurrently modification to the structure is happened by writing the data into the structure. for loop are not
designed to identify the structural modification that is happening concurrently while reading the data from the structures , iterators are capable of 
identifying the concurrent modification and can stop reading by generating concurrent modification exception because iterators are capable of identifying 
concurrent modification and are designed to fail in performing reading operation. Iterators are also called as failfast. 

If reading should happen without generating an exception then instead of using array we have to make use of copyOnRght ArrayList. In general instead of 
classes present in java.util package we have to make use of java.util.concurrent package.

